# NPC standee lock (Tomas bevel v19)

Canonical construction: `assets/npcs/tomas_standee_bevel_v19.png` (option 3 routed wood-sign).

Every **current and future** generated character uses this exact physical design. Change clothes, face, **pose**, props, and name — not the oak construction.

## Variety (required on every new character)

The bevel is the lock. **The figure is not.** Do not clone the last NPC.

**Do not default to** the Nessa/Beph template: over-the-shoulder look-back, matching brown lace-up boots, matching tooled satchel, same hip charm-belt.

**Must vary from whoever is already in the game:**
- Stance (front, 3/4, walking, seated, hands busy — not always looking back)
- Silhouette and costume family (gown vs coat vs work clothes vs Club kit)
- Footwear and bags (or no bag)
- Held object (fan of cards, pipe, stall goods, nothing)

Oak board, wood foot, one ALL-CAPS plaque, no HUD nameplate — those stay. Repeating pose + boots + bag is a miss even if the face is new.

**Must match Tomas:**
- Painted figure on a **chunky routed oak board** that follows the silhouette
- Visible **wood-grain edge / bevel** (highlight top-left, darker grain bottom-right)
- **Rectangular stained-wood foot**, not a circular cobblestone pedestal
- **One wood plaque** on the foot: four small corner rivets, name once in **black serif ALL-CAPS** (TOMAS, NESSA, BRAM, ELIRA, BEPH)
- Isolated sprite; production shots use **lime green `#00FF00` chroma**, then knock out alpha
- No blue/gold HUD nameplate, compass badge, extra diorama base, or doubled lettering
- In-game: hide HTML nameplates; the plaque on the art is the name

**Do not** invent a new outline, cardboard halo, paper-doll tab, or stone plinth unless Marc unlocks this.

Nessa, Bram, Elira, and Beph live cutouts use the Tomas v19 routed oak lip/foot (`*_standee_bevel_v25.png`, Beph `*_v3.png`). Placement and Mark spots are done.

**In-game placement:** each location has four standing anchors with their own size (foreground larger, back smaller). Do not shrink every standee when more people are present. Place every new screen with the **Mark spots** tool (see `location-anchor-tool.mdc`).
